        <mxCell id="n18" value="upload" style="endArrow=open;endFill=0;dashed=1;html=1;strokeColor=#666666;fontSize=11;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n5" target="n9"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n19" value="Three things this diagram states:&lt;br&gt;1. The API keeps NO state, so it can be replicated. Everything that used to&lt;br&gt;   live in process memory — cache, rate-limit counters, socket lists — is in Redis.&lt;br&gt;2. Exactly ONE worker. Cron inside the API would run the reconciliation job&lt;br&gt;   three times; for a job that touches money that is a serious bug.&lt;br&gt;3. Images are not on the VPS disk. Required for replication, and so a redeploy&lt;br&gt;   does not wipe them." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=6;fontSize=11;fillColor=#fffbe6;strokeColor=#c8a415;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="640" width="700" height="120" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
